  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Crlp/1598/2022 on 9 March, 2022 Author: D.Ramesh Bench: D. Ramesh The Hon'Ble Sri Justice D. Ramesh Criminal Petition No.1598 Of 2022 Order:",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioners would submit that this is a covered matter in view of the earlier common order passed by this Court in Criminal Petition Nos.5421 of 2019 and batch, whereby this Court has [LEAKAGE_MASK] several F.I.Rs registered for the similar offences based on identical facts. Therefore, he would submit that the petitioners are similarly placed and they are also entitled for quash of the F.I.R registered against them, leaving the offence punishable under Section 34(A) of A.P. Excise Act, to be investigated. 4. Learned Additional Public Prosecutor fairly concedes that this is a covered matter in view of the aforesaid common order passed by this Court and thereby prayed to pass appropriate orders accordingly in this Criminal Petition also.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioners would submit that this is a covered matter in view of the earlier common order passed by this Court in Criminal Petition Nos.5421 of 2019 and batch, whereby this Court has [LEAKAGE_MASK] several F.I.Rs registered for the similar offences based on identical facts. Therefore, he would submit that the petitioners are similarly placed and they are also entitled for quash of the F.I.R registered against them, leaving the offence punishable under Section 34(A) of A.P. Excise Act, to be investigated. 4. Learned Additional Public Prosecutor fairly concedes that this is a covered matter in view of the aforesaid common order passed by this Court and thereby prayed to pass appropriate orders accordingly in this Criminal Petition also.",
